      "description": "Watch FC Cincinnati vs San Jose Earthquakes highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. A high-stakes MLS encounter on August 2, 2026 , delivered a footballing masterclass in drama as FC Cincinnati faced off against San Jose Earthquakes . The fans were treated to a spectacle that showcased the unpredictable nature of the league, with the lead changing hands in a gripping contest. First Half: Tactical Battle and Quick Exchanges The match ignited in the 26th minute when Timo Werner turned provider, setting up Daniel Munie for a clinical finish to give San Jose Earthquakes the lead. The visitors' joy was short-lived, however, as FC Cincinnati fought back with determination. Just seven minutes later, Evander Ferreira showcased his vision by finding Bryan Ramirez , who slotted home the equalizer. The first half ended in a stalemate, but the intensity suggested that much more was to come after the break. The Late Surge and Cincinnati's Triumph Ten minutes into the second half, San Jose Earthquakes regained their advantage. Preston Judd delivered a perfectly weighted ball to Timo Werner , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net for 1-2. As the clock ticked down, FC Cincinnati unleashed a wave of attacking pressure. In the 79th minute, Tom Barlow leveled the scores once again, assisted by the ever-present Evander . The momentum had firmly shifted, and in the 82nd minute, Evander himself turned scorer, capitalizing on an Obinna Nwobodo pass to put the hosts ahead for the first time. In the dying moments, the tension boiled over with yellow cards for Evander and Miles Robinson , but the home side remained focused. Deep into stoppage time, at 90+5, substitute Ayoub Jabbari put the result beyond doubt, finishing a move started by Tom Barlow to make it 4-2. It was a stunning turnaround that sent the home crowd into raptures and secured three hard-earned points."
